iomat-tools
===========

Tools for interacting with the Realtek RTS5911 iomatrix device:

  o iomat-update - update EC (and other) firmware over the iomatrix device node
  o iomat-mem     - memory access helper for the iomatrix device


EC firmware image
-----------------

The EC main image is installed to the rootfs at:

    /usr/share/iomat-tools/EC_Main_Image.bin

The on-disk name is kept stable so iomat-update can reference a fixed
path.  Each time the EC image is updated, the new bin is tracked in this
repository by its upload date.  Replace EC_Main_Image.bin and add a row
below.


Version history
---------------

Bins are identified by upload date.

2026-09-01
    - Add IO expander I2C slave protocol, GPIO table init, I2C master
      interrupt module (oem_i2cm), and ERRLOG region
    - Add peripheral event callbacks and interrupt status bits for ADC,
      TACHO, I2C master, and ACPI IBF
    - Add GPIO interrupt report (EC GPIO state changes can be reported
      for host/SoC monitoring)
    - Add in-band EC flash update from SoC (iomat-update erases and
      writes via the iomatrix interface)
    - Enhance iomatrix services: PECI OOB forwarding, Port80 interrupt
      forwarding to the snoop channel, PM IBF interrupt bits
    - Align iomatrix protocol stack with Linux: KCS state machine now
      driven by IBF interrupt forwarding, IRQ bitmap aligned
    - Fix: restore LDN UART after eSPI reset


Usage
-----

Update EC firmware using the installed image:

    iomat-update -m rts5911 /usr/share/iomat-tools/EC_Main_Image.bin

See 'iomat-update --help' for all options (device node, model selection).
